@* ============================================================
   AUTHOR: PlantSafety Platform
   CREATED: 2026-08-03
   FILE DESCRIPTION: Admin Portal customer-onboarding quick-start checklist (Phase 7 §6.2
     Customer Onboarding). Deliberately thin: navigation/UX scaffolding pointing at real
     existing pages, not new business logic. ProvisionTenantCommand already seeds default
     reference data during provisioning (Phase 7 §2.1) -- this page does not duplicate that.
   SchemaVersion: 2026.1
   Additive-only evolution — see Enterprise Architectural Rule Handbook §XI
   ============================================================ *@

@page "/admin/onboarding"

@inject NavigationState NavState

<PageTitle>Quick-Start Checklist — PlantSafety</PageTitle>

<div class="ps-page-container">

    <ErrorBoundaryComponent Message="The onboarding checklist could not be displayed.">

        <CardComponent Title="New Tenant Quick-Start Checklist">
            <p class="ps-text-muted">
                A guided sequence of the first real actions a new tenant should take. Each step
                links to the actual page that performs it — nothing here is a simulated or
                sample-data-only walkthrough.
            </p>

            <ol class="ps-checklist">
                <li>
                    <strong>1. Provision the tenant.</strong>
                    Runs the real end-to-end pipeline (Tenant record, data isolation, seeded
                    default reference data, initial admin user, roles, API key).
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.AdminTenantProvision" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Provision Tenant</a>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>2. Confirm the subscription plan and usage limits.</strong>
                    Review the plan resolved for the tenant on the Billing tab of its detail page.
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.AdminTenantList" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Tenant Management</a>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>3. Invite additional users.</strong>
                    Use the tenant's Administrative Setup → Users &amp; Roles tab once signed in
                    as the tenant's admin user (created during provisioning).
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.AdminSetup" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Administrative Setup</a>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>4. Create the tenant's first work item.</strong>
                    Start with an Incident Management record, a Safety Program, or a Workflow
                    approval — whichever matches the tenant's primary use case.
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.IncidentManagementList" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Incident Management</a>
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.SafetyProgramsList" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Safety Programs</a>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>5. Review enabled modules and feature flags.</strong>
                    Confirm the tenant's module/feature-flag configuration matches its plan.
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.OperationsConfigurationDashboard" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Feature Flags</a>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>6. Bookmark the Support Console.</strong>
                    For future support requests: tenant quick-links, audited impersonation, and
                    the tenant's audit stream.
                    <a href="@RouteDefinitions.AdminSupportConsole" class="ps-btn ps-btn-ghost ps-btn-sm">Support Console</a>
                </li>
            </ol>

            <div class="ps-alert ps-alert--info" role="note">
                <span class="bi bi-info-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                Recommendation: a dedicated in-product tutorial/sample-data seeding pipeline
                beyond what <code>ProvisionTenantCommand</code> already seeds is a reasonable
                future enhancement, not built here to keep this checklist proportionate to its
                actual scope (navigation scaffolding, not new business logic).
            </div>
        </CardComponent>

    </ErrorBoundaryComponent>

</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        NavState.SetContext(
            pageTitle: "Quick-Start Checklist",
            activeModuleCode: string.Empty,
            breadcrumbs:
            [
                new BreadcrumbItem { Label = "Main Menu", Href = RouteDefinitions.Home },
                new BreadcrumbItem { Label = "Quick-Start Checklist" }
            ]);
    }
}
